| library/probability/conditional-expectation.md: def-conditional-expectation-given-a-sigma-algebra, thm-tower-property-of-conditional-expectation, thm-conditional-expectation-is-the-l2-orthogonal-projection, def-conditional-variance, cor-conditional-variance-decomposition | Conditional expectation/tower and variance decomposition under actual integrability/AC conventions. |
| library/probability/conditional-distributions-and-regular-conditional-probability.md: def-measure-kernel-and-probability-kernel, def-composition-of-probability-kernels, lem-kernel-composition-is-well-defined-and-associative, thm-existence-of-regular-conditional-distributions-for-standard-borel-targets, thm-disintegration-of-a-joint-law-on-standard-borel-spaces, thm-conditional-density-formula | Pointwise probability-kernel semantics and valid composition of specified kernels; RCD/disintegration and conditional densities. Kernel composition is not for unspecified almost-everywhere classes and is not a causal/missingness assumption. |
| library/probability/markov-kernels-and-markov-chains.md: def-conditional-independence-given-a-sigma-algebra | Published definition by factorization of conditional expectations of bounded measurable functions, up to a.s. equality; inherits AC through conditional-expectation existence. This supplies CI notation used in causal, censoring, missingness and event-process contracts but does not derive any DAG implication. |
| library/probability/independence-borel-cantelli-and-zero-one-laws.md: def-independent-random-elements, thm-independent-random-elements-have-product-joint-law, thm-factorization-of-expectations-for-independent-variables | Independence means independence of the generated sigma-algebras; a finite mutually independent random-element family has product joint law. Pairwise independence is not mutual independence. |
| library/probability/central-limit-theorems.md: def-multivariate-normal-law, lem-characteristic-function-of-a-multivariate-normal-law, thm-lindeberg-levy-iid-central-limit-theorem, thm-lindeberg-feller-central-limit-theorem-sufficiency, thm-multivariate-iid-central-limit-theorem; library/probability/characteristic-functions-inversion-and-continuity.md: lem-characteristic-functions-under-affine-maps-and-independent-sums, thm-uniqueness-of-a-law-from-its-characteristic-function, thm-cramer-wold-device | Gaussian law and scalar projection characterization, affine transforms/independent-sum characteristic functions and law identification (AC where stated); iid/triangular-array limits remain conditional on their own hypotheses. MSF-35 supplies named orthogonal-product and exact t/F clauses. |
| library/probability/weak-convergence-tightness-and-representation.md: def-standard-normal-and-normal-laws, lem-normal-density-has-total-mass-one | Scalar normal laws and density normalization; the normal-law definition is homed here rather than on the CLT page. Positive variance is required for exact Student/F denominators. |
| library/probability/strong-laws-of-large-numbers.md: thm-kolmogorov-iid-l1-strong-law | An iid integrable sequence has sample averages converging almost surely to its mean under the page's stated hypotheses. Used only for the almost-sure termination proof of the iid two-boundary SPRT. |
| library/probability/characteristic-functions-inversion-and-continuity.md: thm-cramer-wold-device | Under AC, convergence of every scalar projection to the projections of a specified finite-dimensional law proves vector weak convergence; used with the martingale score limits in SME-42. |
| library/probability/modes-of-convergence-for-random-variables.md: def-convergence-in-distribution-for-real-random-variables, thm-slutsky-for-real-random-variables, thm-continuous-maps-preserve-convergence-in-probability | Limit modes, scalar Slutsky and continuous mapping. |
| library/probability/discrete-time-martingales.md, library/probability/martingale-inequalities-and-convergence.md, library/probability/stopping-times-and-optional-stopping.md: def-filtration-and-filtered-probability-space, def-martingale-submartingale-and-supermartingale, def-martingale-difference-sequence, def-square-integrable-martingale-difference-array-and-variance-clock, thm-martingale-central-limit-theorem, thm-optional-sampling-for-bounded-stopping-times, thm-azuma-hoeffding-inequality | Discrete-time martingales, scalar terminal CLT and bounded optional sampling. No continuous-time counting-process compensator, jump integral or functional CLT. |
| library/probability/brownian-motion-construction-and-continuity.md and library/probability/the-ito-integral-with-respect-to-brownian-motion.md | Continuous-time filtration/adaptation/predictability definitions and Brownian Itô items; Brownian isometry is not counting-process isometry. |
| library/probability/infinite-product-measures-and-kolmogorov-extension.md: def-stochastic-process-and-finite-dimensional-distributions, def-standard-borel-space, lem-finite-products-of-standard-borel-spaces-are-standard-borel, thm-kolmogorov-extension-for-standard-borel-coordinate-spaces; library/probability/markov-kernels-and-markov-chains.md: thm-ionescu-tulcea-construction-of-a-markov-chain | Finite products preserve standard-Borel structure. Under AC, Ionescu–Tulcea constructs the unique path law with prescribed finite-prefix iterated laws from an initial law and a sequence of arbitrary history-dependent probability kernels; it is not restricted to time-homogeneous kernels. Kolmogorov extension assumes AC and standard-Borel coordinates. Neither supplies path continuity, an observation equation or a filter. |
| library/probability/stationary-markov-chains-and-ergodic-limits.md: def-stationary-process-and-canonical-shift, thm-stationary-process-birkhoff-ergodic-limit | A.s./L1 averages under strict stationarity, integrability and AC; only ergodicity makes the limit constant. No dependent-data CLT or weak-stationarity definition. |
| library/fourier-analysis/bochner-inversion-and-plancherel-on-lca-groups.md: def-positive-definite-function-on-an-abelian-group, thm-bochner-theorem-for-lca-groups | Continuous positive-definite LCA function corresponds to finite positive Radon measure on the dual. Density additionally requires absolute continuity. |
| library/linear-algebra/inner-product-spaces-and-orthogonality.md: thm-least-squares-solutions-and-normal-equation, thm-orthogonal-projection-is-the-unique-nearest-point, thm-qr-factorisation-over-r-or-c; library/linear-algebra/the-spectral-theorem-and-singular-value-decomposition.md: cor-real-spectral-theorem-for-self-adjoint-endomorphisms, thm-courant-fischer-min-max-principle, thm-singular-value-decomposition; library/linear-algebra/the-moore-penrose-pseudoinverse-and-regularised-least-squares.md: thm-a-plus-b-is-the-unique-minimum-norm-least-squares-solution | Projection, QR/SVD, LS minimizers, minimum norm and eigenvalue min-max. No statistical identifiability or sampling law. |
| library/linear-algebra/matrix-differentiation-and-first-order-spectral-perturbation.md: prop-matrix-differentials-obey-sum-product-and-adjoint-rules, thm-derivative-of-matrix-inversion, thm-determinant-differential-and-jacobis-formula, prop-gradient-of-a-quadratic-matrix-form | Matrix derivatives/local perturbation; not finite Davis–Kahan or IRLS convergence. |
| library/measure-theory/lebesgue-stieltjes-measures-and-distribution-functions.md: thm-lebesgue-stieltjes-correspondence-with-distribution-functions, thm-interval-formulas-and-atoms-for-lebesgue-stieltjes-measures; library/measure-theory/measures-and-their-basic-properties.md: def-measure, def-counting-measure, prop-counting-measure-is-a-measure | Distribution/measure dictionary and arbitrary-set counting measure; not random locally finite counting measures or Palm laws. |
| items/ex-characteristic-functions-of-bernoulli-binomial-and-poisson-laws.md | Published example states the scalar Poisson mass $\operatorname{Pois}(\lambda)\{k\}=e^{-\lambda}\lambda^k/k!$, $k\ge0$, including $\lambda=0$. Reuse this count-law convention when defining Poisson process counts; the example supplies no random counting measure, independent-count process, Cox law or point-process theorem and is not a page dependency. |

No existing library page supplies statistical experiment definitions, survey inference, treatment-assignment tests, causal identification, GLM inference, survival estimators, Poisson/Cox process laws or point-process likelihoods, multiplicity procedures or time-uniform validity. Continuous-time event-process prerequisites are new Category-2 suppliers below.

**Existing-supplier assumption ledger.** The item bodies were checked rather than inferred from their titles. All listed suppliers are currently published. Uses of def-multivariate-normal-law, the iid and martingale CLTs, the martingale, conditional-expectation and conditional-independence definitions, RCD/disintegration, and Cramér–Wold inherit their stated Axiom of Choice hypotheses; uses of thm-bochner-theorem-for-lca-groups inherit both AC and DC; uses of the Lebesgue–Stieltjes correspondence inherit Countable Choice. Carry these assumptions and exact item dependencies into consumers that use the clauses. The continuous-time Itô items define Brownian integrals only; SME-30 supplies the new counting-process integral contract.

