## Added prerequisites and remaining limitations

SME-30 is the minimum local Category-2 counting-process compensator/integral/bracket supplier; it precedes survival and point-process consumers that use those operations. SME-31 is the minimum terminal independent-subject influence CLT wrapper; it precedes pointwise KM/logrank/Cox limits. Consumers prove their own influence expansion and random-risk-set remainder. No functional martingale CLT, process bands, Brownian-Itô substitution, or discrete-time-CLT substitution is allowed. No Category-1 interface remains; models-01 reconciled MSF-35's six Gaussian clauses. Remaining local proofs are explicit item-authoring obligations, not an unverified external fallback.

All six model dossiers, source manifests and progress records are complete. models-01 records 19 acquisitions/17 completed focused units, with partial Ch. 5/6 ranges in its manifest; GLM deviance gap remains. Dossiers distinguish read units from extracted, partial and unused material; no whole-book reading is claimed beyond recorded units.

Claim limits retained: no generic GLM saturated-model chi-square/deviance residual law; fixed-design nonidentical GLM asymptotics require a local triangular-array proof, not silent MSF iid transfer. Survival notes refer general process proofs elsewhere; finite-support KM is proved in read Yu pages, while continuous-time limits require local risk-set/influence proof. Cox scores are not called iid before risk-set replacement. Competing-risk source is slide-level; no Aalen–Johansen limit. Currie/IUPAC official PDF returned HTTP 403; detection values use three NIST pages. Agreement has one full primary source and no endpoint coverage. Unsupported ACVF/periodogram, spatial and point-process asymptotics are excluded. Also excluded: invalid finite-site kriging rank inference, Schoenberg converse and Cox directing-law uniqueness whose proof cites an unread analytic-uniqueness result. Models-02 source errors corrected: SRS covariance sign, PPS example arithmetic, finite-population normality, and ICC wording.

There is no unresolved source-coverage, Category-1 interface, dependency-boundary, or assigned-topic blocker to this prose scaffold. Pair count is **62 proposed A/B pairs (124 proposed pages)**, reflecting the new earlier event-process prerequisites and separation of materially different proof routes, not the initial 20-pair draft or literal sum of reader subproposals. No tests, gates, workflow transitions, canonical-plan edits, commits or publications were performed.
